---
description: Core architecture constraints
alwaysApply: true
---
- Treat docs/PRD.md as product source of truth.
- Follow docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for boundaries.
- Separate crawler, extraction, rendering, dynamic discovery, editing, change tracking and persistence.
- Use strict TypeScript.
- Keep domain/application logic independent from Dexie.
- Use repository interfaces.
- Stable content IDs are required.
- Dynamic content is state-aware.
- Treat crawled HTML/CSS/URLs as untrusted.
- Isolate snapshot styling/DOM from application UI.
- Support LTR, RTL and mixed direction.
- Add tests for meaningful behavior.
- Do not weaken security controls for convenience.
